      "writtenOn": "2026-03-24T14:26:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not inclined to land more code for AVX512 given it being disabled on many newer Intel CPUs and activating AVX512 can cause surprising knock-on performance impacts because devices that do support AVX512 might then lower their clock significantly in order to run the 512 instructions, negatively affecting all the other instructions we execute.",
      "revId": "4defa4797a8584d24c956eefcf5b6afb53d4ddec",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c8e411b_caed3cac",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4727287
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-08T06:35:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consistent performance improvements are observed on Intel platforms.\nIntel platforms:\n\nTiger Lake (i5-8250U, UHD 620)\n\nAVX512:\n- Before: 6580.807 ms\n- After : 5737.445 ms   (~13% faster)\n\nAVX2 / Default SSE version\n- No significant change (within noise)\n\n\nIce Lake (i5-1035G1, UHD)\n\nAVX512:\n- Before: 8473.315 ms\n- After : 8199.523 ms   (~3% faster)\n\nAVX2 / Default:\n- No meaningful improvement (within noise)\n\nSummary:\n- Consistent improvements observed on Intel AVX-512 platforms:\n  - Tiger Lake: ~13% speedup\n  - Ice Lake: ~3% speedup",
      "parentUuid": "c6ac6a97_0d185339",
      "revId": "4defa4797a8584d24c956eefcf5b6afb53d4ddec",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
